      {
        "title": "Show HN: I got tired of btop not seeing my Mac's chip, so I built siltop",
        "link": "https://github.com/CLoaKY233/siltop",
        "description": "<p>btop is beautiful. But on my M-series Mac it can't tell me the one thing I actually want to know: what is the chip doing? No watts, no GPU, no per-core clocks.<p>So I built siltop: btop's calm, with eyes on the silicon. Real power, clocks and temps straight from the SMC and IOReport, no sudo, about 1.3% of one core (btop is ~2.5% on the same machine).<p>It also tells you what's wrong in plain words (\"Busy: rustc using 9.1 cores\", \"Hot: fans at 80%\") before you read a single graph.<p>10-second try, no load needed:<p><pre><code>  brew install cloaky233/tap/siltop && siltop --demo\n</code></pre>\nRust, MIT/Apache, no telemetry, no network unless you turn on update checks.<p>Curious what your Mac shows. M1/M2 Ultra and M5 Max owners especially, I haven't seen yours yet.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50128654\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50128654</a></p>\n<p>Points: 5</p>\n<p># Comments: 2</p>",
        "pubDate": "Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:01:07 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50128654"
      },
